# 3.4. Pathways that block PSC-CM maturation

PSC-CMs, in vitro, may have dysregulated signaling or gene expression that prevents them from maturing. Inhibition of the mTOR signaling pathway with Torin1, for example, increases the proportion of quiescent PSC-CMs and expression of maturation related genes [103]. Functionally, treatments with Torin1 improves contractile force, contraction dynamics, and mitochondrial function. Inhibiting mTOR
